<rml>
<head>
	<title>vector strokes</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="/folio/folio.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="/ui/vectors.rcss"/>
	<style>
		/*
			Strokes baked as area, since a distance field has no notion of a line.

			strokes.svg is one of each case the stroker has to get right, and each is checked by
			eye against the shape it is supposed to be:

			  the rectangle       a ring, with the middle open. Baked solid, it would read as a
			                      filled box and hide whatever it was drawn over
			  three triangles     miter, round and bevel joins, which must look different
			  two zigzags         butt and round caps
			  the curve           square caps, and a stroke that follows a bezier
			  the ragged line     the case that used to fail: many short segments turning sharply,
			                      which the old rectangle-per-segment stroker unioned into a solid

			Re-bake both test drawings together with:

			  msdfbake vector --in Tools/uipreview/tests/vectors/wide.svg
			                  --in Tools/uipreview/tests/vectors/strokes.svg
			                  --out Tools/uipreview/tests/ui/art
			                  --rcss Tools/uipreview/tests/ui/vectors.rcss --layers
		*/
		body
		{
			background-color: #101014;
			color: #e8e8f0;
			font-family: Inter;
			font-size: 13dp;
			padding: 16dp;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			box-sizing: border-box;
		}

		p { margin-bottom: 6dp; }

		.big { width: 560dp; margin-bottom: 16dp; }
		.small { width: 180dp; }
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<p>joins, caps, and a ring that must stay open in the middle</p>
	<div class="strokes-stack big">
		<img class="strokes-frame" sprite="strokes_frame"/>
		<img class="strokes_0-ink" sprite="strokes_0"/>
		<img class="strokes_1-ink" sprite="strokes_1"/>
		<img class="strokes_2-ink" sprite="strokes_2"/>
		<img class="strokes_3-ink" sprite="strokes_3"/>
		<img class="strokes_4-ink" sprite="strokes_4"/>
	</div>

	<p>the same at a size where a stroke is a couple of pixels</p>
	<div class="strokes-stack small">
		<img class="strokes-frame" sprite="strokes_frame"/>
		<img class="strokes_0-ink" sprite="strokes_0"/>
		<img class="strokes_1-ink" sprite="strokes_1"/>
		<img class="strokes_2-ink" sprite="strokes_2"/>
		<img class="strokes_3-ink" sprite="strokes_3"/>
		<img class="strokes_4-ink" sprite="strokes_4"/>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
